WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.340
- [Narrator] Side note, no bread makers

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.390
were injured in the making of this video.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.860
As you can probably gather,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.970
this is not your average bread maker.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.170
Nor is this your average bread oven.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.210
Nor is it your average bread.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.610
This is shotis puri, and in Georgian

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.963
that translates to, well, bread.

00:01:04.643 --> 00:01:07.990
- A tonir oven is essential
to the making of shotis puri.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.180
After the oven is built
and the heat is turned up

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.760
to the highest level
for six to seven hours,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.960
the walls of the oven are
covered in a salt based liquid.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.570
And diving in to get the
bread as close to the fire

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.163
is just a part of the job.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.870
- As if diving into a clay
pot isn't intense enough,

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:33.260
this thing hits temperatures

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.040
of 750 to 900 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.630
The end result is a special
bread with a salty twist

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.390
that's eaten on special occasions,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.323
like birthdays, weddings,
Christmas and New Years.

00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:53.596
(bright music)

